#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:139
msgid "Trust Network Participant Verifier"
msgstr "信任网络参与方验证方"

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:143
msgid "Trusted Service"
msgstr "可信服务"

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:97
msgid "Universal verifier applications that support different credential standards are complicated by wide variability in format of the credential payloads, signatures, key formats, and key distribution methods. Public keys formats include x509 certificates, JSON Web Key Sets (JWKS), and DID documents. Signing key distribution methods include API gateways, hosted by issuer at a pre-defined URL, embedded in certificates, and by block-chain based resolution. Establishing root of trust by trust anchor or distributing trust list has been accomplished by API gateway, hosted URL, private dissemination and other bilateral sharing agreements."
msgstr "支持不同凭证标准的通用验证方应用程序，因凭证载荷格式、签名、密钥格式和密钥分发方法差异很大而变得复杂。公钥格式包括 x509 证书、JSON Web 密钥集（JWKS）和 DID 文档。签名密钥分发方法包括 API 网关、由签发方托管于预定义 URL、嵌入证书中，以及基于区块链的解析。通过信任锚建立信任根或分发信任列表，已通过 API 网关、托管 URL、私下传播及其他双边共享协议得以实现。"

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:148
msgid "Verifiable Digital Health Certificate"
msgstr "可验证数字健康证书"

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:149
msgid "Verifiable Digital Health Certificate: A digital representation of a data set comprising a certificate or document, designed for a set of specific clinical or public health use cases which is defined using open, interoperable digital health standards; that contains within, or is associated to, a digital signature which can be verified by the public key of a public-private encryption key pair, and which is issued by a GDHCN Participant."
msgstr "可验证数字健康证书：由证书或文件构成的数据集的数字表示形式，面向一组特定的临床或公共卫生用例而设计，并采用开放、可互操作的数字健康标准加以定义；其内部包含或关联一个数字签名，该签名可通过一对公私加密密钥中的公钥进行验证，并由 GDHCN 参与方签发。"

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:99
msgid "While some variability is expected in an approach that preserves sovereignty, there are opportunities for alignment in key format and distribution for the sake of fostering interoperability. With that goal, we provide a unifying trust list format to assemble and share public key infrastructure for all credential specifications used by existing trust networks. Importantly, this format does not enforce a particular policy framework for participants of the trust network."
msgstr "在维护主权的方法中，预计会存在一定的差异，但为促进互操作性，在密钥格式和分发方面仍有协调统一的机会。为此，我们提供一种统一的信任列表格式，用于汇集和共享现有信任网络所使用的所有凭证规范的公钥基础设施。重要的是，该格式并不对信任网络参与方强制实施特定的政策框架。"
